# Taxonomy references this cluster provides, read at run time by the amplicon
# job (see _amplicon_ref_db_prelude in portal/app/slurm.py). Install as
# ${OMC_DB_DIR}/amplicon_taxonomy.tsv.
#
# Tab-separated: name, path, ranks.
#   name   what the run and the viz call this reference
#   path   absolute, or relative to ${OMC_DB_DIR}
#   ranks  the rank names this reference uses, comma-separated; blank for the
#          pipeline's defaults. They belong here because they are a property of
#          the reference file, and differ between releases — PR2 5.x inserted
#          Subdivision, which 4.x did not have.
#
# Order matters. The first row is the primary reference: renormalization and the
# ASV-level labels come from it, and the others are carried alongside. A row
# whose file is not present is skipped with a warning, so this file can list
# everything the site curates and each cluster contributes what it holds.
#
# name	path	ranks
silva	silva_db/SILVA_138.2_SSURef_NR99.fasta	Domain,Phylum,Class,Order,Family,Genus
pr2	pr2_db/pr2_version_5.1.1_SSU_dada2.fasta	Domain,Supergroup,Division,Subdivision,Class,Order,Family,Genus,Species
# SILVA 132 predates the 2021 ICNP renaming, so it says Proteobacteria where
# 138.2 says Pseudomonadota. Kept for comparison against work that used it.
silva132	silva_db/silva_nr_v132_train_set.fa	Domain,Phylum,Class,Order,Family,Genus
